217
00:07:51,550 --> 00:07:53,640
Let me draw the hole.

218
00:07:53,760 --> 00:07:55,303
Here is the glass box,

219
00:07:55,303 --> 00:07:57,210
as it should have been.

220
00:07:57,300 --> 00:07:59,450
Here is what the trustee found.

221
00:07:59,450 --> 00:08:01,510
A gap of about one point six

222
00:08:01,510 --> 00:08:03,140
billion dollars.

223
00:08:03,280 --> 00:08:04,164
On one side,

224
00:08:04,164 --> 00:08:06,330
the American accounts.

225
00:08:06,330 --> 00:08:07,370
On the other,

226
00:08:07,370 --> 00:08:09,880
the money tied to trades abroad.

227
00:08:09,990 --> 00:08:12,440
And thousands of customers waiting

228
00:08:12,440 --> 00:08:13,584
outside.

229
00:08:13,850 --> 00:08:15,959
Then came the long work of getting

230
00:08:15,959 --> 00:08:16,723
it back,

231
00:08:16,723 --> 00:08:19,096
and of deciding who would be held

232
00:08:19,096 --> 00:08:20,751
responsible.

233
00:08:26,417 --> 00:08:27,467
Piece by piece,

234
00:08:27,467 --> 00:08:31,027
the trustee paid customers back in stages.

235
00:08:31,027 --> 00:08:32,815
By November twenty thirteen,

236
00:08:32,815 --> 00:08:34,824
the securities customers had their

237
00:08:34,824 --> 00:08:36,227
property back.

238
00:08:36,427 --> 00:08:38,003
By April twenty fourteen,

239
00:08:38,003 --> 00:08:40,797
he announced a final distribution.

240
00:08:40,927 --> 00:08:41,806
In total,

241
00:08:41,806 --> 00:08:44,286
about six point seven billion dollars had

242
00:08:44,286 --> 00:08:46,541
gone back to more than twenty-six thousand

243
00:08:46,541 --> 00:08:47,817
customers.

244
00:08:48,097 --> 00:08:48,333
In his words,

245
00:08:48,333 --> 00:08:49,277
they were made one hundred percent whole.

246
00:08:49,277 --> 00:08:50,244
The biggest group,

247
00:08:50,244 --> 00:08:52,416
about twenty-four thousand American

248
00:08:52,416 --> 00:08:53,778
futures customers,

249
00:08:53,778 --> 00:08:55,752
received about five point four billion

250
00:08:55,752 --> 00:08:56,567
dollars.

251
00:08:56,567 --> 00:08:58,882
It had taken about two and a

252
00:08:58,882 --> 00:08:59,996
half years.

253
00:09:00,250 --> 00:09:01,696
In twenty thirteen,

254
00:09:01,696 --> 00:09:04,881
a federal court order required MF Global's

255
00:09:04,881 --> 00:09:07,087
brokerage to pay one point two one

256
00:09:07,087 --> 00:09:09,782
two billion dollars in restitution to

257
00:09:09,782 --> 00:09:10,738
customers,

258
00:09:10,738 --> 00:09:13,899
plus a one hundred million dollar penalty,

259
00:09:13,899 --> 00:09:16,595
to be paid only after the customers

260
00:09:16,595 --> 00:09:17,930
had been paid.

261
00:09:18,280 --> 00:09:21,245
The regulator later said restitution had

262
00:09:21,245 --> 00:09:24,354
been paid to satisfy all customer claims.

263
00:09:24,617 --> 00:09:27,239
And in January twenty seventeen,

264
00:09:27,239 --> 00:09:30,126
Jon Corzine settled the regulator's civil

265
00:09:30,126 --> 00:09:30,967
case.

266
00:09:31,037 --> 00:09:32,864
He agreed to pay a five million

267
00:09:32,864 --> 00:09:35,097
